From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HOTTY Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 18:52:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/23] hottyterm: no tabs, and windows and full screen are the
 window manager's
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Tabs are plx's, and windows and full screen belong to the window
manager (the maintainer, 2026-10-10). Default keys for tabs (new, close,
previous/next, by number, move, the overview), for quitting, for closing
windows and for full screen are gone. The Mac keeps Cmd+Q, Cmd+W and
Ctrl+Cmd+F, which no window manager gives there.

A new tab, from a binding, a menu or `+new-tab`, is a new window. GTK:
the menus lose their tab items, the header bar's button is New Window
and the tab overview button is hidden. macOS: windows never group as
tabs, even with the system's "prefer tabs" setting, and the File menu
loses New Tab and Close Tab.

hottyterm stops keeping tab, close-window and close-all-windows keys
from a surface (SPEC §10.4).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
